## Relationship to Ragin (2008)

Ragin (2008) provides the fsQCA *method*. Fiss (2011) provides the *theoretical rationale* for why fsQCA is the right tool for the causal stage of a typology-building research programme. Together they are the methodological foundation of the fsQCA chapter.

---

## GIQ Rejection Lesson

The GIQ desk rejection (14 April 2026) was diagnosed as a narrative architecture failure. One contributing factor was that P1's SLR was framed as a literature contribution rather than as the first stage of a Fiss-logic configurational programme. When P1 is reactivated for R&G submission (Q3 2027), the Fiss (2011) logic must be foregrounded in §1 — the typology's value is its explanatory potential in the configurational analysis, not the systematic literature review process that generated it.

